Clean-room notice
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The interactive CLI shell under shell/ is a clean-room implementation.

Its design was informed only by the *concepts* and the *public API behaviour* of
the Zephyr RTOS shell (a Linux Foundation project, Apache-2.0) and -- for the
line editor -- by the behaviour of GNU readline / linenoise / bash.  No source
code, comments, or specific wording from Zephyr (or any of those projects) was
copied.  Zephyr was used as a design reference only; none of its code is present
in this repository.

All shell sources (shell/, svc/, and the per-board glue under boards/) are
original work under the MIT License, carrying the header:

    SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
    Copyright (c) 2026 ThreadX Shell Project


Third-party components fetched as submodules
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The firmware is built from, and at runtime incorporates, the components below.
They are git submodules under lib/ (fetched at configure time) and keep their own
licenses -- that code is NOT redistributed in this repository, only referenced.
See each submodule's own LICENSE for the authoritative terms.

Which of them a given image contains depends on the board; boards/<board>/
submodules.cmake is the list that board builds against.

- STMicroelectronics STM32F7xx HAL driver  -- BSD-3-Clause
    lib/stm32f7xx_hal_driver/LICENSE.md    (f746g-disco)
- STMicroelectronics STM32H7xx HAL driver  -- BSD-3-Clause
    lib/stm32h7xx_hal_driver/LICENSE.md    (wio-lite-ai)
- STMicroelectronics CMSIS Device F7       -- Apache-2.0
    lib/cmsis_device_f7/LICENSE.md         (startup, system_*, device headers)
- STMicroelectronics CMSIS Device H7       -- Apache-2.0
    lib/cmsis_device_h7/LICENSE.md         (device headers; the wio-lite-ai port
    supplies its own SystemInit)
- ARM CMSIS-Core                           -- Apache-2.0
    lib/cmsis_core/LICENSE.txt             (both boards)
- Eclipse ThreadX                          -- MIT
    lib/threadx/LICENSE.txt
    A project of the Eclipse Foundation (donated by Microsoft from Azure RTOS);
    the sources carry both Microsoft and Eclipse copyrights.
- Eclipse ThreadX FileX / LevelX / GUIX / NetX Duo  -- MIT
    lib/filex/LICENSE.txt, lib/levelx/LICENSE.txt, lib/guix/LICENSE.txt,
    lib/netxduo/LICENSE.txt
- STMicroelectronics OV5640 BSP component  -- BSD-3-Clause
    lib/ov5640/LICENSE.md
    Sensor register driver for the B-CAMS-OMV camera module on f746g-disco,
    driven by the clean-room glue under boards/f746g-disco/port/camera/.
- TinyUSB                                  -- MIT
    lib/tinyusb/LICENSE                    (wio-lite-ai USB CDC console)
- FlashDB                                  -- Apache-2.0
    lib/flashdb/LICENSE                    (wio-lite-ai key/value store)
- EEMBC CoreMark                           -- Apache-2.0
    lib/coremark/LICENSE.md
    Run as the shell `coremark` command.  CoreMark(R) is a registered trademark
    of EEMBC; see lib/coremark/LICENSE.md (CoreMark Acceptable Use Agreement) for
    the trademark terms.
- MLCommons Tiny (MLPerf Tiny)             -- Apache-2.0
    lib/mlperf-tiny/LICENSE                (wio-lite-ai, opt-in benchmark harness)

The ARM GNU (arm-none-eabi) toolchain is downloaded into ./tools at build time
and is not redistributed as part of this repository.  The same is true of the
tflite-micro tree fetched by the optional tflm NN backend.


Third-party material vendored into this repository
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Two things are in the tree and ARE redistributed in both source and binary form,
so their notices are reproduced here as their licenses require.

1. boards/<board>/port/coremark/core_portme.{c,h}
   Derived from EEMBC's barebones CoreMark port (Apache-2.0, lib/coremark).  Each
   board adapts the timing and reporting hooks; the benchmark itself is compiled
   from the submodule.

2. boards/wio-lite-ai/port/camera/ov2640_regs.c -- OV2640 QVGA RGB565 registers
   The register table in this file is data taken verbatim from STMicroelectronics'
   OV2640 camera component driver:

       https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/stm32-ov2640  (v1.0.3, ov2640.c)

   Only the `OV2640_QVGA[][2]` array is reused.  None of that driver's code is:
   boards/wio-lite-ai/port/camera/camera.c walks the table with its own
   error-checked SCCB writes.  Its license requires the following.

